# Frozen wire-equivalence hashes for the builtin native documents.
# Re-frozen 2026-10-21: the multicast route's schema declares the lock-anchor
# trio, and the wire digest covers declared keys even when absent, so the
# 5.15 multicast profile's bytes changed while no value did.
# Re-frozen 2026-10-25: kernelsnitch.mm_struct_sz returned to the profile
# schema (written only from a measurement), so the digest covers the declared
# key again and every document's bytes changed; no bundled value did.
# Re-frozen 2026-10-27: the bundled profiles carry their measured/known
# mm_struct stride (5.10 = 960, 5.15/6.1 = 1024, 6.6/6.12 = 1280; the
# 6.x values are QEMU-confirmed and replace the null/default).
# Re-frozen 2026-10-29: stage-3 layout facts (cred usage/uid/security,
# rt_mutex_size, waiter_layout) entered the wire schema. They are absent
# on the bundled profiles, so no value changed, but the digest covers
# every declared key and every document's bytes changed.
# Re-frozen 2026-10-29 (bundle fix): the 6.1 profiles take the BTF cred
# values from credential-6_1.conf (copy 128, caps 40); the 5.15 profiles
# keep the 5.x template block (copy 176, caps 48, four reference slots).
# Their bytes still carry the declared stage-3 keys, absent on both.
# Re-frozen 2026-10-30: page-free Stage 1 added the `selinux` (enforcing,
# initialized) and `w1_scratch` (image) wire sections. They are absent on
# the bundled profiles, so no value changed, but the digest covers every
# declared key and every document's bytes changed; the schema digest moved
# to 0x28706e4538054d46.
# Re-frozen 2026-10-30 (Stage 4): the eight bundled 5.10 profiles carry the
# page-free blocks -- `selinux` (enforcing 0, initialized 2) and `w1_scratch`
# (the in-anchor slot on 136/209/226/236; bm_pmd on 81/177/198; the Samsung
# array's zero gap on 101). Only those eight documents changed.
# Re-frozen 2026-10-31: the compat select carrier added three declared
# `route.select_stack` keys (compat_carrier, waiter_home, select_dst_depth).
# They are absent on every bundled profile, so no value changed, but the
# digest covers every declared key: only the select_stack documents' bytes
# moved (the sigreturn 5.10.81/101 documents are unchanged).
# Re-frozen 2026-11-01 (r8): the bundled diting 5.10.81/101 profiles now carry
# the compat select carrier (select_stack with compat_carrier, waiter_home,
# select_dst_depth) instead of the sigreturn route; only those two documents
# changed. 5.10.81 is device-proven (10/10); 5.10.101 remains a QEMU candidate.
